WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.000
Basecamp 5 has a new
and improved text editor,

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.710
and while most of it will be familiar,

3
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.110
there are a few big updates
I want to share with you.

4
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.870
First, Basecamp now supports tables,

5
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.570
so anywhere you can add
text, you can add a table.

6
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.140
To do that, just look for
this four square or grid icon

7
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.120
and click on it to add your table.

8
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.030
From here, you can add or remove rows

9
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.180
or columns to get your table
formatted the way you need.

10
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.270
So for this example, let's say
I wanna document some podcast

11
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.720
episodes and the number of
downloads. That makes sense

12
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.170
for a table. You can easily
add that information in

13
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.920
and tab between columns and rows.

14
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.480
This just makes it really easy

15
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.040
to present the information in a

16
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.270
way that makes the most sense.

17
00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.210
Now let's say I already have
this information in a separate

18
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.460
spreadsheet, but I want
to put in Basecamp.

19
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.780
You can easily do that as well.

20
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.760
So let's pop over to this spreadsheet.

21
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.300
I'm gonna copy a few of
those rows and columns,

22
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.870
and then I can post it
directly in Basecamp.

23
00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.630
Support for tables has been
a long time customer request

24
00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.210
and we're so excited to
have it in Basecamp 5.

25
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.180
Now, in addition to tables,
we've also added the ability

26
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.610
to leave voice notes throughout Basecamp.

27
00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.560
So let me jump into this chat.

28
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.470
Instead of typing, you can
now leave a voice note.

29
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:16.740
So you'll see this little
microphone icon, just click it

30
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.150
and start recording.

31
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.610
As soon as you're done, you
can hit the stop button.

32
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.820
You will see a preview of that voice note.

33
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.880
You can even play it back,
click it and start recording.

34
00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.670
As soon as you're done, you
can hit the stop button,

35
00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.100
and then once you post that to Basecamp,

36
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.785
your team can hear the voice note.

37
00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:36.870
Again, a customer request for that.

38
00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.370
Now, last but not least,

39
00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.580
our new text editor
also supports Markdown.

40
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.070
So if that is something
that you are familiar with,

41
00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.340
you can use the Markdown syntax

42
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.080
and Basecamp will
automatically format your text

43
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.700
using Markdown.

44
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.160
We're really excited about
these updates to Basecamp 5,

45
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.150
and we hope you are too.
